\import{base-macros}
\author{kellenkanarios}
\title{Permission and the write are two separate events}
\taxon{Card}
\tag{card}
\meta{anki}{1786316439086}

\prompt{Which two events are conflated in "the store issues a [[GA7N]] request", and which one is required to be post-commit?}{
  \ol{
    \li{\strong{Requesting permission} — GetM/BusRdX/RFO, or an Upgrade if the line is already in S.}
    \li{\strong{Performing the write} — merging the store data into the line, leaving it in M.}
  }

  Only \strong{(2)} is architecturally constrained to be post-commit. Permission can be acquired speculatively, well before the store is known to be real.
}
